[{"id":95472,"sender_id":520,"sender_full_name":"Bruno Stonek","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/57414fb5bab160ff299756cdee943c33?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95472\">#1</a> There is a sentence that is confusing me. I suspect it’s a mistake, or at least I don’t know how to make it work as stated. Right after Remark 2.9 here <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Introduction%2Bto%2BStable%2Bhomotopy%2Btheory%2B--%2B1-1\">Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1</a></p>\n<p>It is stated that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">S</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>→</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma^{p-q-1}\\mathbb{S} \\to X \\to \\hat{X} \\to \\Sigma^{p-q}\\mathbb{S}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.9468em;\"></span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9468em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2523em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1667em;\"><span class=\"mord\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">S</span></span></span></span> is a homotopy cofiber sequence. However, the left square above that is not a homotopy pushout. You cannot replace that disk by a point, just as in the definition of a classical CW-complex you cannot replace the disks by points.</p>\n<p>I’m sorry if this is not the right place to write about this!</p>","timestamp":1638351938,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":95474,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95474\">#2</a> I think the answer is:</p>\n<p>The 1-categorical pushout diagram with the disk is a model for the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-categorical homotopy pushout with that disk replaced by a point.</p>\n<p>Does that answer the question? Otherwise, you may please have to say again what issue you see.</p>","timestamp":1638359651,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":95483,"sender_id":563,"sender_full_name":"Hurkyl","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ff42efa94f111c3f310350c872de031d?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95483\">#3</a> The surrounding context looks like it’s talking about the model category rather than the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-category it presents, so I think that whole section should be interpreted as talking about the model category.</p>\n<p>The thing I think <a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95472\">#1</a> overlooks is that if one leg of the span is a cofibration between cofibrant objects, and the third vertex is cofibrant, you can replace it with anything else that is weakly equivalent and also cofibrant.</p>\n<p>In particular, the homotopy cofiber of a cofibration between cofibrant objects can be given by taking the pushout with the point.</p>","timestamp":1638388360,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":95486,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95486\">#4</a> Yes, that’s what I mean (saying “<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\infty</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>-” instead of “homotopy-“). This is what the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StrictModelStructureCellAttachmentToSpectra\">Rem. 2.9</a> in question is referring to in parenthesis: where it says “hence its homotopy cofiber (<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-1#StrictModelStructureCellAttachmentToSpectra\">def.</a>)”. Here “def.” is <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Theory#HomotopyFiber\">def. 4.16</a> in Part I of the notes. More on this is in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback#HomotopyPullbackByOrdinaryPullback\">Prop. 3.1</a> at <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/homotopy%20pullback\">homotopy pullback</a></em>.</p>\n<p>If that is what <a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95472\">#1</a> is asking about, let me know which kind of clarifying sentence you’d like to see added to the notes.</p>","timestamp":1638425987,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":95493,"sender_id":520,"sender_full_name":"Bruno Stonek","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/57414fb5bab160ff299756cdee943c33?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95493\">#5</a> Thanks for the replies. Hurkyl, I agree that would work. A closely related, alternative justification: the stable model category of spectra is proper, so a pushout is a homotopy pushout as soon as one of the legs is a cofibration, which is obviously the case here.</p>\n<p>I don’t immediately see which of the two justifications would be more appropriate, or less circular.</p>\n<p>I would say that a justification along these lines would clarify the exposition.</p>","timestamp":1638438525,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":95494,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95494\">#6</a> The justification as such is already given, as pointed out in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95486\">#4</a>. What you seem to want is more prose to go with it.</p>","timestamp":1638439268,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":95495,"sender_id":520,"sender_full_name":"Bruno Stonek","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/57414fb5bab160ff299756cdee943c33?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95495\">#7</a> That’s true. I personally think a more verbose explanation would not be pointless: see my confusion in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95472\">#1</a>! </p>\n<p>Now I’m confused by something else there :) Shouldn’t the first term of the homotopy cofiber sequence actually be <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∨</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{S}^{p-q-1}\\vee \\mathbb{S}^{-q}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∨</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>? The second summand appears because of the added disjoint basepoint: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≃</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Σ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>∨</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Sigma^{\\infty}_+S^{p-1}\\simeq \\Sigma^\\infty(S^{p-1}\\vee S^0)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1194em;vertical-align:-0.3053em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3053em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≃</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Σ</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">∞</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">∨</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>","timestamp":1638441751,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":95496,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95496\">#8</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I personally think a more verbose explanation would not be pointless: see my confusion in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95472\">#1</a>!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes, I understand, but I am trying to make you help me see <em>how</em> it should be expanded to be more helpful, since to my eyes all comments are already there. :-) That happens, of course, the author of a text sometimes can’t step back from it far enough. But anyway, I can try to expand. Later, when I have a quiet moment.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Now I’m confused by something else there </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>True, that’s more of a gap in the commentary: Namely the bottom left object is not actually a replacement of the point, either, but is itself a wedge sum of such with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{S}^{-q}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. So that pushout square on the left is really the one we have been discussing, wedged with the cofiber square of the identity on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{S}^{-q}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">S</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>Okay, I’ll look into clarifying that remark a little more. When I find a minute. Thanks for bringing this up!</p>","timestamp":1638443037,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]},{"id":95497,"sender_id":520,"sender_full_name":"Bruno Stonek","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/57414fb5bab160ff299756cdee943c33?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/5-nLab-General-Discussions/topic/A.20homotopy.20cofiber.20sequence.20in.20.22Intro.20to.20stable.20homotopy.20th.E2.80.A6/near/95497\">#9</a> Ah yes, of course, the bottom left object also has the +, so the left square doesn’t obviously present a homotopy cofiber sequence.</p>\n<p>Thanks for looking at it, looking forward to your edit.</p>\n<p>Oh, and as to how to make the previous part clearer: I think it’s in Hurkyl’s comment or mine above, i.e. explicitly remark that those pushouts are actually homotopy pushouts because such-and-such.</p>","timestamp":1638443949,"subject":"A homotopy cofiber sequence in \"Intro to stable homotopy th…","stream_id":5,"display_recipient":"nLab General Discussions","reactions":[]}]